  "history_summaries": [
    "Round 1: Fix bus_gnt_one_hot assertion error. The `assertOneHot` macro checks for exactly one bit set (PopCount===1), but the design correctly allows bus_gnt=00 (idle state) when no queue is requesting. Changed line 249 from `assertOneHot(bus_gnt, \"bus_gnt_one_hot\")` to `fvAssert(PopCount(bus_gnt) <= 1.U, \"bus_gnt_one_hot\")`, which matches the comment's intent (\"at most one grant active at a time\") and the design's arbitration logic (lines 210-216). Assertion label preserved exactly. No homologous assertions found (`assertOneHot` used only once in the file).",
    "Round 2: Fix grant_requires_request assertion_error. Root cause: assertion on line 263 compares registered bus_gnt (updates at clock edge) with combinatorial bus_req (drops immediately when queue empties), causing a one-cycle violation when a queue is serviced and its request drops one cycle before the grant clears. Fix: replace bus_req.orR with RegNext(bus_req).orR to snapshot the previous-cycle request value that caused the grant to be set. Assertion label 'grant_requires_request' preserved exactly. No homologous assertions: inspected lines 252, 255, 258, 261—none have the same !bus_gnt.orR || ...orR structure.",
    "Round 3: Fix no_request_no_grant assertion_error. Root cause: the assertion on line 261 checked `!(bus_req(0)||bus_req(1)) || bus_gnt.orR` which is logically `request→grant` (wrong direction) and compared combinatorial bus_req against registered bus_gnt without acknowledging the 1-cycle delay. Fix: replaced with `!bus_gnt.orR || RegNext(bus_req).orR` which checks `grant→previous_request` — the correct \"no request, no grant\" property with proper pipelining. This matches the pattern already used in the sibling `grant_requires_request` assertion (line 264, fixed in round 2). Assertion label `no_request_no_grant` preserved exactly. No homologous assertions: inspected all assertions — none other than line 261 had the `!(bus_req(0)||bus_req(1)) || bus_gnt.orR` pattern."
  ],
